Z||000008||BroCar 87||11-01-2000||03:23 AM||||Well, I got my car back yesterday. It WAS the oil pressure sending unit as we thought!!! Good shot guys. It cost me $140 (NOT BAD AT ALL) to get all the tests and work done!! I was very pleased with these guys. <BR>That was the good news, now for the bad news. I DO have a lil knock in the valve train now. Also, my car stalls at low RPM's such as at a stop light or slowing down to a stop sign.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I don't have any clue why this is happening. It stalled 5 times on the way home from the shop. Twice today. I don't think I am getting enough gas to keep it on. <BR>Also, I stopped about the QUAD 4 swap at SpeedCraft, which deals alot with that particular engine. And they had no clue on how to do the swap. They did a Caddy N* conversion, but wouldn't really help me out   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Sooo BACK TO SQUARE ONE!!<P>V8 maybe??? More research needed first!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>2xsess: I haven't had a chance to check out that junk yard yet. Ken (the guy that thinks its a mera) said it started with a "m" but seemed longer than 4 letters. I am going to have to check it out in person I believe!<P>Well, I will keep you guys posted on the progress of my dying engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Good luck on your fieros though!!<P>Robert:  hehe my fiero was parked next to yours at the shop  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Sight for sore eyes I tell ya!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>   Custom dual side exit exhaust!||||reg||1
Z||000009||RobertVol||11-01-2000||11:34 AM||||Bro I know a guy that can do the V-8 conversion for ya. You will have to pay for the engine and the kit but he will do the work for little as nothing as long as you help. He loves doing conversions ! not for money just for hobby! I think if interested he could help you out if you want to go that way. Some of his work has already been purchased by a Forum member and he sems pleased so let me know <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||BroCar 87||11-01-2000||12:53 PM||||WOW Rob, thats the best news I've heard about this situation yet. I have looked around and no one wants to even mess with my fiero swaps. Not a Quad 4 swap nor a V6 upgrade... I am getting very discouraged here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I am thinking V8 power is GONNA be the solution   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Sent you an email... thanks for looking out!!<BR>2xsess: nice pic of the side exit dual exhaust....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Bro outt!!!||||reg||10
